  "verbalization": "Calabaxanthone is shown to have a target relationship with DMS-273 through multiple pathways, with the most direct link involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This subunit is targeted by a compound that, in turn, is targeted by DMS-273, suggesting a potential inhibitory effect on the proteasome pathway. The second pathway links Calabaxanthone to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by another compound, Erysimoside, which also targets DMS-273. This indicates that Calabaxanthone may act through a different mechanism, possibly involving Ataxin-2, which is a component of the proteasome and is involved in cellular degradation processes.\n\nThe evidence suggests that Calabaxanthone may exert its effects through a proteasome-related pathway, as it is linked to a subunit of the proteasome and to compounds that target the proteasome. The presence of multiple targets in different pathways supports the idea that Calabaxanthone may act through a complex network of molecular interactions, possibly involving the proteasome and related proteins. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Calabaxanthone to modulate cellular processes through the proteasome, which is a well-established target in various therapeutic contexts. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism involving the proteasome, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
